{"version":3,"term":{"cols":80,"rows":24},"timestamp":1780578209,"command":"npm run demo","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.126, "o", "\r\n> engramx@4.2.0 demo\r\n> tsx demo/run.ts\r\n\r\n"]
[0.214, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1m  engram — the honest before/after\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m  real handler, engram's own repo. nothing staged. (DEMO_FAST=1 to skip pacing)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.902, "o", "\u001b[2m  A developer's agent searches the codebase. Every match line from each\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m  search floods into the model's context window.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.178, "o", "  \u001b[36m\"init\"\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(116 matches)\u001b[0m           \u001b[2m2,376 tok\u001b[0m → \u001b[32m582 tok\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m−76%\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.730, "o", "  \u001b[36m\"query\"\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(178 matches)\u001b[0m          \u001b[2m3,679 tok\u001b[0m → \u001b[32m706 tok\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m−81%\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.730, "o", "  \u001b[36m\"parse\"\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(163 matches)\u001b[0m          \u001b[2m3,440 tok\u001b[0m → \u001b[32m588 tok\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m−83%\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.739, "o", "  \u001b[36m\"getStore\"\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(73 matches)\u001b[0m        \u001b[2m1,356 tok\u001b[0m → \u001b[32m541 tok\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m−60%\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.734, "o", "  \u001b[36m\"Node\"\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(409 matches)\u001b[0m           \u001b[2m7,412 tok\u001b[0m → \u001b[33mpassthrough\u001b[0m  \u001b[2m(engram declines — never worse)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.701, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.602, "o", "\u001b[1m  Structural context on the intercepted searches: 10,851 → 2,417 tokens  (\u001b[32m−78%\u001b[0m)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m  ~4.5× more searching before you hit the context wall.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.001, "o", "\u001b[33m  The asterisks the over-claimers hide:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m  • STRUCTURAL context tokens — not your bill. Prompt caching owns cost;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    engram's net over caching ≈ 0. The win is capacity + ranked quality.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m  • The packet is a RANKED subset (PageRank), and the reductions above are a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    CEILING — they assume the ranked call-sites answer the search with no raw\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m    follow-up. engram always prints the exact `rg -n` to recover the rest;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    real recall-coverage here is ~22%. The honest P-modelled figure: `npm run bench`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  • Selective by design — engram intercepts only ~20% of searches here (the\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m    high-fan-out ones, ≥4 caller files); the rest pass through, never worse.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.901, "o", "\u001b[2m  Reproduce the rigorous aggregate on any repo:  \u001b[0m\u001b[36mnpm run bench\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.009, "o", "⠙"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1G"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[0K"]
[0.003, "x", "0"]
